SUMMARY:In The Other Room: Shaun Weiss
LOCATION:Helium Comedy Club\, 3070 Windward Plaza\, Alpharetta
DESCRIPTION:Shaun Weiss began acting at age six in Bill Cosby’s Jell-O ca
 mpaign and went on to appear in Pee-wee’s Playhouse\, The King of Queens\
 , Boy Meets World and the cult comedy Heavyweights. But he’s best known a
 s Goldberg\, the goalie in Disney’s Mighty Ducks trilogy.\n\nAfter a high
 ly publicized battle with meth and heroin addiction—including arrests\, h
 omelessness and three years living on the streets—Shaun made an extraordi
 nary comeback and has now celebrated seven years in recovery.\n\nToday\, We
 iss has turned those experiences into stand-up comedy\, telling hilarious a
 nd sometimes unbelievable stories about growing up as a famous child actor\
 , surviving homelessness and addiction\, and discovering that somehow Holly
 wood wasn’t the weirdest part of his life.\n\nNow based in Atlanta with h
 is fiancée\, Shaun tours the country performing stand-up\, appearing at fa
 n conventions and sharing his message of recovery\, resilience and never gi
 ving up—even when your IMDb page looks healthier than you do.\n\nHelium C
 omedy Club Alpharetta is proud to be his home club.\n\nThere is a two-item 
 per person minimum in the Showroom\, which can be fulfilled with any food o
 r drink items from the menu.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: Food and drinks purchased in t
 he bar and lounge do not count towards the two-item minimum.\n\nManagement 
 reserves the right to prevent customers from entering the facility who they
  deem disruptive or dangerous to other patrons.\nMore info: https://comedya
 tlas.app/comedy-atlas/event/in-the-other-room-shaun-weiss/
